  <revision rev="19" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>6809744573ceef42a43905fb30016e74</srcmd5>
    <version>3.1.0</version>
    <time>1794591159</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- updated to 3.1.0 (3.001)
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-Data-Dump-Streamer/Changes
  3.001 - 2026-11-10
  Perltidy source to my preferred format. Fixed issues serializing
  the global stash. Added test to detect if serializing the global
  stash breaks anything.
  Fix version assignments so PAUSE can index the distribution.
  3.00 - 2026-11-10
  Rewrite the dumping engine in C/XS, with AI assistance, for improved speed,
  correctness and compatibility with Perl's refcounted stack. Improve Unicode
  and regexp handling, and add experimental support for XPerl class objects.
  CVE-2026-126673 bsc#1290113
  Require Perl 5.18 or newer and a C compiler. Replace Module::Build with
  ExtUtils::MakeMaker.
  There is no pure-Perl version. Please don't upgrade if you need pure-Perl
  support.</comment>
    <requestid>1397120</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="20" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>65df7389f1b61eb0dda0543e491a69c9</srcmd5>
    <version>3.2.0</version>
    <time>1795023135</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- updated to 3.2.0 (3.002)
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-Data-Dump-Streamer/Changes
  3.002 - 2026-11-11
  Fix compilation on Cygwin by declaring private XSUBs with XS_INTERNAL.
  Remove compiler warnings in the XS helpers and add Cygwin CI coverage.
  Support Perl 5.12 and newer, with CI coverage for 5.12, 5.14 and 5.16.</comment>
    <requestid>1398400</requestid>
  </revision>
